{"created": "2026-10-24T22:32:58.970634+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-24T22:32:59.253325+00:00", "id": 23628190, "conceptrecid": "23624432", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23628190", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23624432", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23628190", "metadata": {"title": "Two-strip square packings: improved upper bounds for s(n), n = 1184\u20139944", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23628190", "publication_date": "2026-10-24", "description": "<p>2824 new upper bounds for packing n unit squares in a square (1184 &le; n &le; 9944); 867 of them improve on the trivial grid &lceil;&radic;n&rceil;. Karimi two-strip construction: two low-angle strips of tilted squares attached to the walls (one on the bottom wall, one on the right wall), the rest an axis-parallel grid. All angles have rational tan(&theta;/2), so every certificate is exact (rational coordinates); each passes the exact verifier of Mishapolk/square-packing-records. records.csv lists the new and previous sides and the construction parameters; regenerate.py rebuilds every certificate exactly. Version 2 extends version 1 (683 records, n &le; 3775) to all boxes K = 35&ndash;100; part of the search was run by the author in MATLAB Online. Related theorem: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23627827. Code and computations were done with the assistance of Claude (Anthropic) under the author's direction.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Karimi, Mohsen", "affiliation": "Independent researcher, Zanjan, Iran", "orcid": "0009-0004-1055-8267"}], "keywords": ["square packing", "packing unit squares", "upper bounds", "discrete geometry", "experimental mathematics"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.23627827", "relation": "isSupplementedBy", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}], "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 2, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_t